class Solution {
    public String longestPalindrome(String s) {

        int n = s.length();
        int l=0,r=0;

        if(n<2) return s;

        boolean[][] dp = new boolean[n][n];
        int maxLen=1;

        for(int i=0;i<n;i++){

            dp[i][i]=true;

            for(int j=0; j<i;j++){

                // if the characters at positions i and j are the same and either the length of the substring is less than or equal to 2 (which means it's a palindrome) or the substring between j and i is a palindrome (dp[j+1][i-1] is true), 
                // then we can conclude that the substring from j to i is also a palindrome.  

                if(s.charAt(i)==s.charAt(j) && ( i-j<=2 || dp[j+1][i-1])){ 
                        dp[j][i]=true;

                        if(i-j+1>maxLen){
                            maxLen=i-j+1;
                            l=j;
                            r=i;
                        }

                       
                }
            }
        }

        return s.substring(l,r+1);
        
    }
}

explanation:
- We create a 2D boolean array `dp` where `dp[i][j]` indicates whether the substring from index `j` to index `i` is a palindrome.
- We initialize the diagonal of the `dp` array to `true` since any single character is a palindrome.
- We iterate through the string using two nested loops. The outer loop iterates through the end index `i` and the inner loop iterates through the start index `j`.
- For each pair of indices `(j, i)`, we check if the characters at those indices are the same and if the substring between them is a palindrome (or if the length of the substring is less than or equal to 2, which means it's automatically a palindrome).
- If the conditions are met, we mark `dp[j][i]` as `true` and check if the length of this palindrome is greater than the current maximum length. If it is, we update the maximum length and store the starting and ending indices of this palindrome.
- Finally, we return the longest palindromic substring using the stored indices.    
TC - O(N^2)   SC - O(N^2) (for the dp array)


6. Decode ways

link - https://leetcode.com/problems/decode-ways/

solution

class Solution {
    public int numDecodings(String s) {

        int n= s.length();
        
        int[] dp = new int[n+1];

        dp[0]=1; // if the string is empty, only one way we can decode it
        dp[1]= s.charAt(0)=='0' ? 0 : 1;

        //dp[i] = numbers of ways[i-1](if last digit is valid) + numbers of ways[i-2](if last combination two digit is valid)

        for(int i=2;i<=n;i++){

            int oneDigit =Integer.valueOf(s.substring(i-1,i));
            int twoDigit =Integer.valueOf(s.substring(i-2,i));

            if(oneDigit >= 1 && oneDigit <=9){
                dp[i]+=dp[i-1];
            }  

            if(twoDigit >=10 && twoDigit<=26){
                dp[i]+=dp[i-2];
            }                                                                                                         
            
        }

        return dp[n];
    }
}